{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED exact head 2eb1301cb6f19db9001b3296a3e5ea78ddfce06c, limited to the stage-2 delta. Architecture: the tool catalog does not yet meet the request that every description state its result contract, empty/absent outcome, and workflow position. Concrete examples: tailapp_metrics lists subject matter but never states its returned object shape or empty-engine shape; tailapp_get, tailapp_schema, tailapp_validate, and several mutation tools do not state what absence/empty means (normally an error/no empty successful result); tailapp_status names fields but not the empty apps/unavailable shape. The static orientation test cannot catch these omissions: TestEveryToolCarriesOrientation asserts only nonempty title, byte ceiling, and docs-URI suffix, so it does not pin the claimed result/empty/workflow content. Add complete concise descriptions and a table-driven contract test with per-tool required result, empty/absence, workflow, and safety phrases. Also correct the draftWrite comment: tailapp_install first-activates and does touch materialized state; destructiveHint false is still honest because install is create-only and destroys nothing. Security: annotation mappings themselves are correct and complete, but self-sufficient prose is the fallback for clients that ignore annotations, so inaccurate/omitted lifecycle and empty-state wording affects approval decisions. Simplification: one declarative per-tool orientation table can drive both catalog entries and exact tests instead of semantic requirements living only in prose. Verification: clean exact-head worktree; go test ./..., go vet ./..., go test -race ./..., and ./scripts/demo.sh passed (demo emitted broken-pipe warnings but exited successfully). The stage-1 base has a separate changes-requested verdict; this verdict concerns only stage 2.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:16bce3728d8e5f7514ff757741f1177977e51f5b","head":"2eb1301cb6f19db